spec.section:
### 3. Complete root tree and schema notation

```text
schema_version, namespace
vp { owner, rev, grants { objective_create, message_inject, room_read } }
gateways[] { id, host_id, url, transport, auth_token_ref, max_inflight }
agents[] { id, role, gateway, hermesBinding, identity, workdir, allowed_workdirs,
           skills, tools, runtime, composition, permissions, approvals,
           create_subordinate, max_sessions, max_parallel, responsibility,
           session, triggers, rooms }
workers[] { id, role, gateway, hermesBinding, identity, workdir, allowed_workdirs,
            skills, tools, runtime, composition, permissions, approvals,
            create_subordinate, max_sessions, max_parallel, responsibility,
            temporary, temporary_config }
projects[] { id, workdirs }
hierarchy { manager_creation { enabled, max_director_created, provisioning } }
rooms[] { id, kind, participants }
registry[] { agent, responsibility, mirror_key }
ingress { bind, public_url, credential_ref, max_body_bytes, max_clock_skew_s }
scheduler { enabled, base_url, auth_token_ref, callback_url,
            callback_auth_token_ref, namespace, timezone }
dispatch { transport, admission_authority, max_inflight_per_gateway,
           targets, duplicate_policy }
admission { run_now_owner, scheduler_bump_fallback }
worker { direct_gateway, progress_interval_s, timeout_s }
capacity { per_role, unresolved_hold_s, probe_backoff_s }
crier_bridge { enabled, endpoint, auth_token_ref, board, announce_room, inject_kinds }
ui { enabled, bind, read_scoped, base_path }
duckbrain { base_url, token_dir, health_interval_s }
storage { controller, classes { coordination_report, control_key,
          session_archive, project_code_memory }, tool_class, effective_readback }
archive { namespace, export_trigger, checkpoint_cadence_s, retention_days, read_scopes }
federation { enabled, local_vp_precedence, no_sender_vp, peers[] }
orchestration { max_fanout, stale_after_s }
verify { deadline_s, remind_gap_s, max_reminds, followup_after_s,
         max_followups, wait_timeout_s }
session { fork_policy, resync, restore_policy, per_agent_override,
          per_project_override }
measurement { window_cycles, nonregression_tolerance_pct, steady_state_band_tokens }
```

The fully expanded registry in §8 enumerates every nested key and array/map item. `[]` means each member, `{*}` each typed map value. Empty validation `{}` means only the registered type and universal rules apply; it does **not** allow unknown object fields. Each object is closed except the three maps listed in §2. Schema conditionals are part of the contract, not informational comments.
